{'symbol': 'HON', 'date': '2019-10-17 14:30:00', 'title': 'Honeywell Sees Continued Margin Improvement in Aero Unit In 2020 - Conf Call', 'text': 'HONEYWELL SAYS DOES NOT EXPECT A SIGNIFICANT IMPACT TO THE COMPANY\'S OPERATIONS IN 2019 DUE TO THE GROUNDING OF BOEING\'S 737 MAX JETS.HONEYWELL SAYS IT REMAINS "SOMEWHAT CAUTIOUS" IN ITS OUTLOOK GIVEN THE CONTINUED UNCERTAINTY IN THE MACRO ENVIRONMENT, BUT ADDS THAT FULL YEAR CONTINUES TO BE "SOLIDLY" ON TRACK- CONF CALL.HONEYWELL SAYS IN 2020 GROWTH OUTLOOK FOR THE OVERALL ECONOMY WILL NOT BE AS ROBUST AS IT HAS BEEN IN 2018 AND 2019.HONEYWELL SAYS COMMERCIAL AFTERMARKET ACTIVITY IN 2020 WILL BE DRIVEN BY INCREASES IN FLIGHT HOURS THOUGH AT A SLOWER PACE.HONEYWELL SAYS WILL CONTINUE MARGIN IMPROVEMENT IN 2020 THOUGH LIKELY AT A SLOWER PACE THAN 2019 IN AERO UNIT.HONEYWELL SAYS NONRESIDENTIAL CONSTRUCTION GROWTH WITH SLIGHT MODERATION SHOULD ENABLE CONTINUED DEMAND FOR BUILDING TECHNOLOGIES, PRODUCTS AND SERVICES IN 2020.HONEYWELL SAYS IN PMT UNIT, CO EXPECTS PROCESS AUTOMATION TO CONTINUE TO GROW IN 2020, DUE TO CONTINUED STRONG ORDERS IN BACKLOG.HONEYWELL SAYS IN PMT UNIT, MACRO DATA SUGGESTS THAT THE SOFTER MARKET IN THE U.S. MIDSTREAM OIL AND GAS CONTINUES, WHICH WILL AFFECT THE GAS PROCESSING BUSINESS IN 2020.HONEYWELL SAYS NEGATIVE IMPACT AT ADVANCED MATERIALS FROM ILLEGAL IMPORTS OF HFCS INTO EUROPE WHILE BEING PROACTIVELY ADDRESSED WILL LIKELY CONTINUE INTO 2020.HONEYWELL SAYS IN SPS BUSINESS, PRODUCTIVITY PRODUCTS IS PROGRESSING ON ITS TURNAROUND, AND CO EXPECTS TO RETURN TO GROWTH AND MARGIN EXPANSION DURING 2020.'}
