{'symbol': 'MS', 'date': '2019-10-17 11:30:00', 'title': 'Morgan Stanley Reports Q3 Adj. Earnings Per Share Of $1.21', 'text': 'THIRD QUARTER 2019 EARNINGS RESULTS.MORGAN STANLEY REPORTS NET REVENUES OF $10.0 BILLION AND EPS OF $1.27 IN QUARTER.QTRLY NET INCOME APPLICABLE TO MORGAN STANLEY $1.27 PER DILUTED SHARE.QTRLY INSTITUTIONAL SECURITIES NET REVENUE $5.02 BILLION VERSUS $4.93 BILLION.SAYS DELIVERED STRONG QUARTERLY EARNINGS DESPITE TYPICAL SUMMER SLOWDOWN AND VOLATILE MARKETS.QTRLY WEALTH MANAGEMENT NET REVENUE $4.36 BILLION VERSUS $4.40 BILLION.QTRLY INVESTMENT MANAGEMENT NET REVENUE $764 MILLION VERSUS $653 MILLION.QTRLY COMPENSATION EXPENSE $4.43 BILLION VERSUS $4.31 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.11, REVENUE VIEW $9.60 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AS OF SEPT 30, TANGIBLE BOOK VALUE PER COMMON SHARE WAS $39.73 VERSUS $38.44 AS OF JUNE 30.QTRLY ANNUALIZED RETURN ON AVERAGE COMMON EQUITY WAS 11.2% VERSUS 11.2% REPORTED AT Q2-END.QTRLY EQUITY SALES AND TRADING NET REVENUE WERE ESSENTIALLY UNCHANGED FROM A YEAR AGO.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.11, REVENUE VIEW $9.60 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY NON-COMPENSATION EXPENSES ABOUT $2.90 BILLION VERSUS $2.71 BILLION.QTRLY FIXED INCOME SALES AND TRADING NET REVENUE INCREASED 21% FROM A YEAR AGO.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.21.QTRLY ADVISORY REVENUE INCREASED REFLECTING THE IMPACT OF HIGHER M&A FEES ON AN INCREASE IN THE VOLUME OF TRANSACTIONS.REPORTED NET REVENUE OF $10.0 BILLION FOR Q3 ENDED SEPTEMBER 30, 2019 COMPARED WITH $9.9 BILLION A YEAR AGO.'}
{'symbol': 'MSI', 'date': '2019-10-17 22:30:00', 'title': 'Motorola Solutions Announces the Addition of Ballistics and Crime Gun Intelligence to Its Software Portfolio to Bring Greater Efficiency and Speed to Law Enforcement Investigations', 'text': 'Motorola Solutions announced the addition of ballistics and crime gun intelligence to its software portfolio to bring greater efficiency and speed to law enforcement investigations. The addition is made possible through the powerful combination of Vigilant BallisticSearch™, which provides enhanced ballistics image capture and analysis, and Vigilant CrimeSearch™, a new pattern crime mapping, data retrieval and analysis tool. When deployed together, the two solutions enable law enforcement to connect seemingly disparate crimes to identify patterns, expedite case closures and improve public safety. BallisticSearch is a portable hardware and software solution that allows law enforcement personnel to capture, analyze and compare 2-D images of fired cartridge casings (FCCs), so they can triage FCCs for identification of unique firearms and generate real-time investigative leads. The system can be deployed at the agency, within criminal laboratories or on-site at crime scenes. It offers a virtual correlation center, providing agencies with access to senior firearms examiners to perform forensic analysis of cartridge casings. The solution is priced at a fraction of the cost of traditional computerized ballistics imaging systems to help close gaps in the use of ballistics intelligence and accelerate crime investigations.'}
