{'symbol': 'PM', 'date': '2019-10-17 09:30:00', 'title': 'Philip Morris International Inc. Reports 2019 Third-Quarter Results', 'text': 'PHILIP MORRIS REPORTS 2019 THIRD-QUARTER RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.22 EXCLUDING ITEMS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.36 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.20.REVISES ITS FULL-YEAR 2019 REPORTED DILUTED EPS FORECAST TO BE AT LEAST $4.73.QTRLY CIGARETTE AND HEATED TOBACCO UNIT SHIPMENT VOLUME DOWN BY 2.1%.QTRLY NET REVENUES UP BY 1.8%; UP BY 7.0% ON A LIKE-FOR-LIKE BASIS, EXCLUDING CURRENCY.PHILIP MORRIS INTERNATIONAL - HAD CHARGE OF APPROXIMATELY $0.20 PER SHARE RELATED TO AN EXCISE TAX AND VALUE ADDED TAX (VAT) AUDIT IN RUSSIA IN Q3.QTRLY NET REVENUES $7,642 MILLION , UP 1.8%.INCREASED REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND BY 2.6% TO AN ANNUALIZED RATE OF $4.68 PER COMMON SHARE.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $7.67 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.21 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY ADJUSTED DILUTED EPS, EXCLUDING CURRENCY, GREAER THAN OR EQUAL TO $5.28.FORECAST EXCLUDES CONTEMPLATED PROPOSAL TO END CIGARETTE PRODUCTION IN BERLIN, GERMANY, BY JAN 2020.PHILIP MORRIS - APPROXIMATELY 950 EMPLOYEES ARE ANTICIPATED TO BE IMPACTED UNDER CONTEMPLATED PROPOSAL TO END CIGARETTE PRODUCTION IN BERLIN.EXPECT OUR NET REVENUE AND ADJUSTED OPERATING INCOME GROWTH IN Q4 TO BE IN LINE WITH OUR YEAR-TO-DATE RESULTS.PHILIP MORRIS INTERNATIONAL - ON TRACK TO DELIVER TARGET OF FULL-YEAR CURRENCY-NEUTRAL, LIKE-FOR-LIKE ADJUSTED DILUTED EPS GROWTH OF AT LEAST 9%.'}
{'symbol': 'PM', 'date': '2019-10-17 22:30:00', 'title': 'Philip Morris International Inc. Reports Consolidated unaudited Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Philip Morris International Inc. announced consolidated unaudited earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 20,380 million compared to USD 20,439 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 2,788 million compared to USD 3,156 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,896 million compared to USD 2,247 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.22 compared to USD 1.44 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 58,072 million compared to USD 59,965 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 8,025 million compared to USD 8,675 million a year ago. Net income was USD 5,569 million compared to USD 6,001 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 3.57 compared to USD 3.85 a year ago.'}
